WEBVTT

00:04.730 --> 00:06.690
How absolutely revolting.

00:07.070 --> 00:10.110
Not only do they constantly stand in the 
way of our noble Eastern Expedition,

00:10.110 --> 00:16.120
they kidnap our heroes, 
besmirching humanity's glorious history.

00:16.830 --> 00:20.020
When they are mere barbarians, 
living beyond the light of civilization.

00:23.480 --> 00:24.890
It's the bird again!

00:24.890 --> 00:28.130
But we can't put up much of 
a fight with this equipment.

00:38.920 --> 00:41.650
Fear not.

00:41.650 --> 00:47.320
We carry with us the most 
potent of God's miracles.

00:47.320 --> 00:49.770
More than enough to vanquish some beast.

00:49.770 --> 00:52.700
Be that as it may, 
Retinue Priest Malcius,

00:52.700 --> 00:55.650
if we don't resupply soon, 
our chances of surviving...

00:55.650 --> 00:57.350
You want to run back to base, is that it?

00:58.180 --> 01:00.770
You gentlemen are knights 
of the Eastern Expedition.

01:00.770 --> 01:03.000
I thought that meant honorable,
distinguished service.

01:03.430 --> 01:04.790
But if your efforts

01:04.790 --> 01:07.770
end in no better results than the 
expedition from 20 years ago...

01:10.840 --> 01:13.960
There is only one way to avoid such shame:

01:15.450 --> 01:19.290
the rescue of Lady Serafina de Lavillant!

01:19.290 --> 01:21.470
For both your honor as knights

01:21.470 --> 01:23.430
and so that the The Order of Commoneras

01:23.430 --> 01:27.000
can see our long-held dream 
of eastern conquest fulfilled!

01:45.920 --> 01:53.510
The Warrior Princess and the Barbaric King

03:22.810 --> 03:24.600
What a fine edge.

03:25.100 --> 03:27.800
That should do for today's firewood.

03:27.800 --> 03:29.850
Really? We're done already?

03:30.110 --> 03:34.980
You say that, but in the past three 
days, you've cut two weeks' worth.

03:35.390 --> 03:38.810
If all I do is eat and sleep, 
my body will lose its edge.

03:38.810 --> 03:42.740
And I obviously want to familiarize 
myself with such a fine weapon.

03:44.360 --> 03:47.000
Should I take that to mean your 
restlessness from the past few days

03:47.000 --> 03:49.620
has been due to boredom, then?

03:51.230 --> 03:54.100
So much time without any 
meetings or exercise...

03:54.100 --> 03:57.500
is quite the change of pace 
from how my life used to be.

03:57.500 --> 04:01.520
And yet, you've never helped 
with household tasks before.

04:01.520 --> 04:07.410
Honestly, I should have done my share 
of that sort of thing as a squire...

04:09.150 --> 04:10.550
But my grandfather

04:10.550 --> 04:13.940
apparently put some degree of pressure 
on the knight I apprenticed to.

04:14.460 --> 04:17.900
The idea of a major noble bending 
the rules like that is scary.

04:18.190 --> 04:22.130
Well, I doubt you'll be bored today.

04:22.700 --> 04:25.310
Considering... Oh, look.

04:30.370 --> 04:35.920
Hey, Sera! Care to spar with 
the village's warriors?

04:38.730 --> 04:44.550
He mentioned some bright idea he 
had to resolve your frustration.

04:44.550 --> 04:47.090
I wasn't expecting something 
so... meat-headed.

04:47.090 --> 04:50.930
Look how many of them there are! 
I can't just send them away.

04:50.930 --> 04:52.850
Oh, well!

04:52.850 --> 04:54.560
Speaking of meatheads...

04:54.820 --> 04:58.560
Sorry, Cersei, but could 
you bring Sera's armor out?

04:58.560 --> 05:01.320
Sure! Just a moment.

05:04.600 --> 05:08.060
You had my armor all along?

05:08.520 --> 05:11.900
Once it was off of you, 
I wiped the blood and mud away,

05:11.900 --> 05:14.430
but I've only done the bare 
minimum of daily maintenance.

05:14.860 --> 05:16.580
No. That should suffice.

05:21.560 --> 05:24.090
I suppose the helmet couldn't be fixed.

05:24.390 --> 05:26.550
I'll help you put it on.

05:26.550 --> 05:28.260
You know how?

05:28.260 --> 05:30.250
More or less.

05:30.250 --> 05:33.470
Considering I was the 
one who took it off you.

05:34.750 --> 05:37.990
Most can't remove and equip
 armor without experience...

05:53.170 --> 05:54.610
I apologize for the wait.

05:55.160 --> 05:57.500
I am a knight commander of 
the kingdom of Illdoren...

05:57.720 --> 06:01.170
But you know me better 
as the Crystal Helmet.

06:01.890 --> 06:03.500
Let's see if you can 
alleviate my boredom!

06:06.460 --> 06:09.750
Getting to fight the Crystal Helmet... 
It's like a dream!

06:09.750 --> 06:11.760
Me! I wanna go first!

06:12.030 --> 06:13.740
There's no need to rush.

06:15.270 --> 06:17.770
We'll be doing this 
with wooden swords, Sera.

06:19.700 --> 06:20.890
I thought as much.

06:26.270 --> 06:29.540
Our first challenge for the famous 
Crystal Helmet is the young warrior

06:29.540 --> 06:33.190
who experienced battle for the first 
time in the most recent conflict...

06:33.190 --> 06:37.040
Warrior Raham, son of 
Gamelan, the Blue Fang!

06:40.040 --> 06:43.040
Comport yourselves with honor, and begin!

06:43.040 --> 06:45.070
Don't hold back on my account!

06:49.080 --> 06:50.850
Raham!

06:50.850 --> 06:53.550
He said not to hold back!

06:53.770 --> 06:56.560
Next is Gamelan the Blue Fang!

06:56.560 --> 06:59.630
I will avenge my boy's little boy...

06:59.630 --> 07:02.380
as his father!

07:03.300 --> 07:06.350
My own little boy!

07:04.740 --> 07:06.350
Dad!

07:06.350 --> 07:09.570
You both fight the same way!

07:10.540 --> 07:12.410
Let me go next.

07:12.410 --> 07:15.450
Very well. Next is Two-Necked Sero!

07:17.820 --> 07:18.930
Crystal Helmet.

07:19.460 --> 07:21.270
First, I want thank you.

07:22.700 --> 07:24.880
When the Tsukebikeshi 
attacked the village...

07:25.640 --> 07:28.360
you protected my sister and nephew.

07:30.010 --> 07:31.470
They're your family?

07:31.690 --> 07:35.140
I'm grateful that you kept 
Yufa and Gatar alive.

07:35.960 --> 07:38.470
That said, the spar's a separate matter.

07:38.730 --> 07:40.400
Show no restraint!

07:40.400 --> 07:41.350
Right.

07:42.340 --> 07:43.180
Here I come!

07:50.750 --> 07:54.270
Gamelan and Sero were both 
taken down with ease!

07:55.740 --> 07:57.370
Now I'm really fired up!

08:04.880 --> 08:07.140
Sh-She's so strong.

08:07.140 --> 08:09.520
These are all skilled warriors, but...

08:09.520 --> 08:14.130
Well, considering how much willpower 
Illdoren is using, it's no surprise.

08:14.550 --> 08:18.910
Lady Vyufumec, Master Veor 
explained it to me before

08:18.910 --> 08:21.640
but I'm still not sure 
what this "willpower" is.

08:21.940 --> 08:24.270
It's not that complicated.

08:30.300 --> 08:33.050
Willpower is just what it sounds 
like; the strength of one's will.

08:33.400 --> 08:36.410
Their desire to achieve something.

08:36.910 --> 08:39.830
Birds being able to fly, 
fish being able to swim,

08:39.830 --> 08:43.420
dragons being powerful, 
we Tefyu being as free as we are,

08:43.420 --> 08:45.010
it all comes from the same source.

08:46.570 --> 08:51.920
We Tefyu don't have flowing 
blood or bodies of flesh.

08:52.340 --> 08:57.620
We're sort of the living dreams of the 
wind, water, clouds, earth, and flames.

08:58.780 --> 09:03.140
The Ixt, Quefto, and Kufuwek 
all have bodies of flesh,

09:03.140 --> 09:05.010
but have long, long lifespans.

09:06.830 --> 09:11.690
But... the Cornem live 
for such a short time.

09:13.060 --> 09:17.440
With not nearly enough time to 
accomplish the things they want to.

09:17.440 --> 09:22.620
Which is why Cornem warriors have 
such strong, strong willpower.

09:23.350 --> 09:27.120
It sharpens their technique, 
increases their strength,

09:27.120 --> 09:28.960
and gives life to 
their fighting techniques.

09:29.210 --> 09:33.710
And techniques strengthened with willpower
can only be contested with willpower.

09:34.090 --> 09:37.930
Then if their martial and 
physical prowess are both equal,

09:37.930 --> 09:41.050
it's willpower that determines 
who wins a fight?

09:41.050 --> 09:42.220
Right.

09:42.220 --> 09:46.850
That powerful desire to accomplish 
something in their brief lives...

09:47.350 --> 09:51.860
It's something that seems truly 
dazzling to the rest of us.

09:52.260 --> 09:54.690
It almost seems to shine.

10:07.430 --> 10:09.850
It's a draw!

10:13.830 --> 10:15.630
It seems I didn't manage to win.

10:15.630 --> 10:21.140
Seeing how I lost last time, 
I could hardly risk doing so again.

10:21.700 --> 10:25.840
What? Are you still worried 
about what I said the other day?

10:25.840 --> 10:27.640
Oh, no...

10:28.010 --> 10:30.650
But how about it? Did that 
help ease your boredom?

10:30.650 --> 10:34.230
Yeah! I'm feeling pretty 
relieved right now.

10:34.230 --> 10:35.650
And I have you to thank.

10:38.430 --> 10:41.320
And this after they were fighting 
seriously seconds ago...

10:41.670 --> 10:44.850
Now, that was some lively willpower!

10:44.850 --> 10:47.040
There's nothing I enjoy more.

10:47.040 --> 10:49.700
A Tefyu being impressed 
with someone else's vigor...

10:49.700 --> 10:52.900
Is that why you're visiting today?

10:52.900 --> 10:55.050
Some booze would make 
the outing even better.

10:55.050 --> 10:58.050
Hey! We've got trouble!

10:58.050 --> 10:59.370
What's wrong?

10:59.980 --> 11:04.070
We've got an injured Morisuberi heading 
this way from the western woods!

11:04.070 --> 11:05.310
What?!

11:05.620 --> 11:08.140
Is it another dragon?

11:20.540 --> 11:24.320
From what I can tell, these dragon 
attacks are out of the ordinary.

11:25.700 --> 11:30.140
But it's strange. The Tsukebikeshi 
around here don't approach villages.

11:30.140 --> 11:33.080
They've learned how they'll 
be attacked, if they do.

11:33.330 --> 11:36.770
The Tsukebikeshi incident, and now this...

11:38.100 --> 11:41.380
From what the other lookouts tell 
me, it's not just this Morisuberi!

11:41.380 --> 11:44.690
There's been a bunch of other dragons 
that have injuries from humans!

11:45.090 --> 11:46.570
That's odd.

11:46.570 --> 11:51.600
No one who lives in these parts would 
let a wounded dragon get away...

11:52.120 --> 11:55.110
Something bad is going 
on in the western woods.

11:55.620 --> 11:59.080
It's different from the intense 
look he has during battle.

12:00.200 --> 12:02.470
I didn't expect to see 
such a face on Veor...

12:05.230 --> 12:06.530
I've got a bad feeling.

12:08.310 --> 12:09.120
It's beginning!

12:25.470 --> 12:26.050
This way!

12:33.080 --> 12:34.310
Now tie it down!

12:36.410 --> 12:37.310
Sera!

12:37.530 --> 12:38.570
I've got it!

12:47.660 --> 12:49.120
Nicely done.

12:55.170 --> 12:58.510
The Crystal Helmet finished it off!

13:05.340 --> 13:08.110
Hey, I could use some rope!

13:08.110 --> 13:09.960
What'll we do with the tail?

13:09.960 --> 13:12.140
It won't be enough, at this rate.

13:12.470 --> 13:14.190
That's one big dragon...

13:14.190 --> 13:15.720
It's a Morisuberi.

13:15.720 --> 13:20.600
Unlike the Tsukebikeshi and other flying 
dragons, it's a type of True Dragon.

13:20.600 --> 13:24.040
True Dragons? What is the difference?

13:24.040 --> 13:28.110
The number of legs. See how it has six?

13:28.110 --> 13:33.790
According to Ixt sages, 
the center pair used to be wings.

13:34.430 --> 13:38.040
In the distant past, 
they apparently flew via willpower.

13:39.330 --> 13:42.350
Something this heavy used to fly?

13:42.710 --> 13:45.920
That really would be like a dragon 
from out of a fantasy tale.

13:45.920 --> 13:49.050
There are other breeds whose 
wings are still intact.

13:49.330 --> 13:52.490
The Fire Dragon that dwells in the 
Quefto's mountains, for example.

13:52.490 --> 13:55.550
That sounds even more fantastical.

13:56.950 --> 13:59.560
Hey! Come take a look at this!

14:00.580 --> 14:02.570
Here's the wound we heard about.

14:02.820 --> 14:06.240
It's a burn, but it 
looks odd, doesn't it?

14:06.240 --> 14:08.960
It's pretty deep, but there's 
not much soot at all.

14:08.960 --> 14:10.570
Ordinary flame didn't do this.

14:11.370 --> 14:14.860
It reminds me of the Rijutsu 
that the Ixt use...

14:14.860 --> 14:18.280
Rijutsu? Is that some kind of magic?

14:18.280 --> 14:19.080
It is.

14:19.540 --> 14:24.840
Normally, for burns, it'd require some 
sulfur or volcanic stone as a catalyst.

14:24.840 --> 14:29.220
But if that was the case, 
there'd be more charring...

14:29.220 --> 14:32.780
Sera, are there people in the west 
who use this kind of sorcery?

14:32.780 --> 14:34.170
In Illdoren?

14:34.170 --> 14:37.850
I can say for certain that no 
one of these lands did this.

14:37.850 --> 14:42.260
I can't think of anyone in the 
Eastern Expedition who uses magic...

14:44.750 --> 14:46.660
Wait. Could it be?

14:47.860 --> 14:50.030
Did someone come to mind?

14:53.160 --> 14:58.050
The clergy of the Order of Commoneras, 
from the western kingdoms.

14:58.550 --> 15:02.190
A number of them have accompanied the 
Eastern Expedition as retinue priests.

15:03.210 --> 15:06.670
Their duty is to perform simple 
masses and funerary writes with the

15:06.670 --> 15:11.240
power of light in camps to soothe the 
spirits of the eastern knights...

15:12.260 --> 15:17.130
But I've never heard of their miracles 
having any combat potential.

15:17.130 --> 15:20.640
Illdoren! Orkfiem! There's trouble!

15:20.640 --> 15:25.900
The Ixt have found the maniacs who've 
been using Rijutsu without a catalyst!

15:25.900 --> 15:29.240
Are they mad?! 
They're actually doing such a thing?

15:29.240 --> 15:31.780
And because of that, a blight 
will be showing up any time now!

15:32.380 --> 15:33.400
A blight?

15:34.060 --> 15:36.080
Hear me well, warriors!

15:36.080 --> 15:38.650
Excluding those with second names,

15:38.650 --> 15:40.670
I want half of you to collect 
and clean the dragon!

15:41.050 --> 15:44.290
The rest are to return to the village 
and prepare for the worst-case scenario!

15:44.940 --> 15:48.030
Those who have a second name, 
brace yourselves, and come with me!

15:50.020 --> 15:52.300
Veor, what are these blights?

15:52.540 --> 15:56.560
Blights are what happens when 
natural law becomes stagnate.

15:56.560 --> 15:59.800
They become antithetical to the natural 
world... Fiends, in other words.

16:00.890 --> 16:01.970
Fiends?

16:03.100 --> 16:07.160
There is a type of monster... 
we call them Fiends.

16:07.160 --> 16:09.230
As you live here, you'll 
encounter them sooner or later.

16:09.230 --> 16:12.070
They're a bit like a living disaster.

16:23.770 --> 16:26.710
We cannot turn back after 
having come so far.

16:27.500 --> 16:29.820
No matter what price we must pay...

16:31.700 --> 16:32.850
This way!

16:53.930 --> 16:55.250
Malcius!

16:57.770 --> 16:59.780
Retinue Priest Malcius!

16:59.780 --> 17:02.000
Lady Serafina?

17:02.520 --> 17:06.510
Lady Serafina! You're not hurt!

17:07.320 --> 17:08.740
Lady Lavillant!

17:09.660 --> 17:13.630
They don't seem like they'd be completely 
incompatible with our way of life...

17:15.140 --> 17:17.140
Sera, do you know them?

17:17.140 --> 17:20.260
She was the priest assigned to 
my First Division of knights.

17:20.260 --> 17:23.870
L-L-Lady Serafina!

17:23.870 --> 17:27.980
That savage! He's one
of those wretched barbarians!

17:27.980 --> 17:29.400
He needs to die!

17:29.620 --> 17:33.470
Calm yourself, Malcius. 
Do not be so wantonly aggressive.

17:33.570 --> 17:34.900
Consider your situation.

17:34.900 --> 17:36.150
You say that, after all this time?!

17:36.840 --> 17:42.650
We have been warring for 700 years... 
This is the 17th expedition!

17:42.650 --> 17:45.290
Justice is with those of us from the east!

17:45.290 --> 17:48.540
How could the Lavillant 
princess have forgotten this?!

17:50.540 --> 17:55.730
Did these lowborn creatures violate you?!

17:55.730 --> 17:57.800
No! It's not like that!

17:58.090 --> 18:00.590
Damned barbarians!

18:01.180 --> 18:04.830
Omgab! Feu louv! Vefshiv!

18:04.830 --> 18:06.180
Am Fyuek!

18:06.620 --> 18:08.690
Stop it! What do you think you're doing?!

18:08.690 --> 18:09.770
In Vif!

18:13.310 --> 18:15.880
That must've been what 
injured the Morisuberi.

18:16.310 --> 18:18.700
Then the source of the commotion...

18:18.700 --> 18:22.210
Did you see that, Lady Serafina?!

18:22.210 --> 18:23.730
In these foul barbarian lands,

18:23.730 --> 18:28.080
God's miracles have grown 
all the more potent!

18:28.380 --> 18:32.090
What could this prove other than our 
righteousness?! We are righteous!

18:32.420 --> 18:35.050
Of all the asinine mistakes to make.

18:35.050 --> 18:36.720
You should not take such pride

18:36.720 --> 18:38.970
in absconding with the power 
of the earth and the trees.

18:42.020 --> 18:46.980
Come, Lady Serafina. 
Let's return home together.

18:54.430 --> 18:56.160
What's the matter?

18:56.160 --> 19:00.610
Malcius, is it? For Sera's sake, 
I'm going to ask only once...

19:00.830 --> 19:03.060
Can we not discuss this matter?

19:03.060 --> 19:06.210
Stop talking, you savage!

19:09.170 --> 19:11.330
Wait! Even if you do this—

19:10.450 --> 19:14.120
I was willing to show mercy by simply
demonstrating God's power,

19:14.120 --> 19:15.420
but you had to get uppity!

19:15.420 --> 19:19.010
So be it! You may feel His 
wrath for yourself, and repent!

19:19.380 --> 19:23.850
Feuk Um! Feu louv! Omgab! Vefshiv!

19:24.090 --> 19:25.430
That fool!

19:25.430 --> 19:26.390
In Vif!

19:34.040 --> 19:35.150
Veor?!

19:37.490 --> 19:39.440
God's wrath finds it's mark!

19:39.440 --> 19:42.160
Come along now, Lady Serafina!

19:46.540 --> 19:48.150
Lukewarm.

19:52.370 --> 19:53.470
Veor...

19:54.900 --> 19:57.260
Your projectiles are not 
nearly enough to pierce armor

19:57.260 --> 19:59.060
that is fortified with willpower.

19:59.590 --> 20:01.670
If you want to kill me...

20:01.940 --> 20:05.680
then take up a blade and use it to 
sever my head from my shoulders!

20:08.620 --> 20:13.190
I was happy to see that you were 
in no rush to return home, Sera.

20:16.830 --> 20:23.950
G-G-Get away from Lady Serafina, 
you ignorant barbarian!

20:23.950 --> 20:28.080
Cease this foolishness, 
before you come to regret it!

20:28.080 --> 20:31.210
Begging for your life will not save you!

20:33.000 --> 20:34.600
Omgab!

20:35.080 --> 20:36.410
Feu louv!

20:37.090 --> 20:40.150
Vefshiv! Feuk Um!

20:41.490 --> 20:42.990
What's happening?

20:43.390 --> 20:46.090
The vitality of the land 
is being used up...

20:46.440 --> 20:49.540
The nature of the earth and 
trees is becoming twisted...

20:51.890 --> 20:56.830
Forgive me, Sera. That woman 
cannot be saved, at this point.

20:58.380 --> 20:59.950
Time is up.

21:01.130 --> 21:05.110
Let God's wrath fall upon the barbarian!

21:08.070 --> 21:09.120
What is this?

21:09.430 --> 21:10.620
Malcius!

21:10.620 --> 21:12.660
Retinue Priest Malcius!

21:14.420 --> 21:19.500
Is this barbarian sorcery?! 
How revolting! Unhand me!

21:19.500 --> 21:21.750
Malcius, I'll save you!

21:22.030 --> 21:23.070
Don't, Sera!

21:23.380 --> 21:24.760
Don't stop me, Veor!

21:24.990 --> 21:29.980
The blame may be hers, but I can't simply 
watch as one of my people is killed!

21:29.980 --> 21:31.760
It isn't a matter of blame.

21:32.100 --> 21:34.770
The blight... has manifested.

21:39.560 --> 21:40.780
No!

21:46.180 --> 21:47.580
That's a Fiend.

21:47.910 --> 21:49.030
A Fiend?

22:02.540 --> 22:05.090
So, this is a Fiend...

22:10.850 --> 22:13.640
Translation: Lee Francis

Timing: Andy Ellis

Editing: Zachary Carlysle

Quality Control: Salem Alabanza

Translation Check: Sho Stifler
